      "content": "It is certainly valid to argue that selective application of sanctions suggests political bias over pure moral concern. Critics frequently point to double standards in how various countries are targeted, suggesting economic pressure serves great power interests rather than universal democratic ideals. This critique views democracy promotion as a secondary justification for enforcing geopolitical agendas shaped by dominant powers. To a large extent, seeing sanctions as a tool of Western hegemony is a persuasive and well-supported perspective in contemporary IR theory.",
